1
00:00:00,260 --> 00:00:03,530
ChatGPT gets about two and a half billion questions a day.

2
00:00:03,640 --> 00:00:04,770
Let's follow just one.

3
00:00:05,000 --> 00:00:06,630
So, can I eat pizza for breakfast?

4
00:00:06,680 --> 00:00:07,170
Send!

5
00:00:07,680 --> 00:00:09,350
Your words become ones and zeros.

6
00:00:09,550 --> 00:00:11,040
The phone's brain packs them up,

7
00:00:11,100 --> 00:00:12,590
and the antenna fires them out!

8
00:00:12,810 --> 00:00:16,160
Zap! To a tower, down a cable of light, into a building full of computers.

9
00:00:16,640 --> 00:00:18,350
Computers only understand numbers,

10
00:00:18,450 --> 00:00:21,920
so your question gets chopped into little LEGO bricks, each with a number.

11
00:00:22,110 --> 00:00:23,820
Then, it reads all the words together.

12
00:00:23,910 --> 00:00:25,050
Pizza, plus breakfast...

13
00:00:25,070 --> 00:00:26,250
a map to a pizza shop?

14
00:00:26,270 --> 00:00:27,520
Nope! A food question.

15
00:00:27,910 --> 00:00:30,100
Here's the surprise: it doesn't look the answer up.

16
00:00:30,210 --> 00:00:33,860
It writes one word at a time, always guessing the most likely next word.

17
00:00:34,030 --> 00:00:35,460
Like: twinkle, twinkle, little...

18
00:00:35,830 --> 00:00:38,740
Star! It learned that by reading a gigantic pile of text.

19
00:00:39,030 --> 00:00:40,760
Then, the answer zooms all the way back!

20
00:00:40,850 --> 00:00:43,040
Technically, yes! Just maybe add some fruit.

21
00:00:43,220 --> 00:00:44,670
All of that, in about two seconds.

22
00:00:45,320 --> 00:00:46,500
It just did that for you...

23
00:00:46,520 --> 00:00:48,910
and about two and a half billion more times today.

24
00:00:49,120 --> 00:00:50,970
And it has never once tasted a pizza.

25
00:00:51,370 --> 00:00:52,280
Follow for more.
